# Merge behaviour for upstream syncs.
#
# Background: this fork tracks 19h/idax. See docs/UpstreamSyncPlaybook.md for
# the full procedure; scripts/sync_upstream.sh applies it.

# ── Generated artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# bindings.rs is bindgen output, checked in only as an offline fallback for
# docs.rs. Merging it textually is meaningless and produces duplicate extern
# blocks; keep our side and let the sync script regenerate it from the merged
# C ABI header.
#
# Requires: git config merge.ours.driver true   (sync_upstream.sh sets this)
bindings/rust/idax-sys/src/bindings.rs merge=ours -diff

# ── Append-only ledgers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These files only ever grow, so union keeps both sides' entries instead of
# forcing a manual resolution. Union is safe here precisely because nobody
# edits or deletes existing entries.
#
# It is NOT safe for prose or tables — see the warning below.
.agents/*.md merge=union

# ── Prose and tables: deliberately NOT union ─────────────────────────────
# README.md, docs/*.md and the binding READMEs get edited and deleted, not
# just appended to. Union silently keeps both sides of every hunk, which:
#   - leaves a current table row next to a months-stale one, and
#   - resurrects content the other side deliberately removed.
# The August 2026 sync hit both: seven duplicated README domain rows, and
# five documents restored with upstream's scrubbed personal paths.
# Let these conflict and resolve them by hand;
# scripts/check_merge_residue.py catches leftovers either way.

# ── Binaries ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# IDA databases and packaged frameworks have no meaningful textual merge.
*.i64 binary
*.id0 binary
*.id1 binary
*.id2 binary
*.nam binary
*.til binary
bindings/swift/Frameworks/** binary

# ── Line endings ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
